-- title:
--   Deligne–Rapoport genus identity at level Γ_H(M), p ‖ M
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, let $H \le (\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ be a subgroup containing every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb Z/M)^\times \to (\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Write $H'$ for the image of $H$ in $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ and $\Gamma_{H'}(M/p) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ for the subgroup of $\Gamma_0(M/p)$ whose lower-right entry reduces into $H'$, as produced by [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133). Then the repartition genus (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor) of the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionField M H`, increased by $1$, equals twice the repartition genus over $\kappa$ of `qExpFunctionFieldC` for $\Gamma_{H'}(M/p)$ — the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\kappa)$ generated by the quotients of $\kappa$-reductions of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for that group — plus the number of pairs $(v,w)$ of places of that field with $w$ satisfying the predicate `IsSSPlaceQExp` for $p$ and $v =$ `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` applied to $w$.
--
--   This is the function-field form of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $p$ of $X_H(M)$ when $p$ exactly divides $M$: the fibre consists of two copies of $X_{H'}(M/p)$ over $\kappa$ crossing at the supersingular points, and constancy of the arithmetic genus in the flat proper family yields the displayed identity. It is used in the study of specialisations of places of $J_H$, in the two results on divisors supported away from, respectively invariant under, inertia at $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_genusFF_xHFunctionFieldBar_add_one_eq_two_mul_genusFF_add_natCard_ssNodePairsQExp.lean

